  "id": "experimental-manipulation",
  "term": "experimental manipulation",
  "definition": "Experimental manipulation is a research method in which investigators deliberately alter a factor in a study, such as social identity or social norms, to test its causal effect on behavior. In this context, the changes were created within a virtual social setting.",
